\f4\b\fs40 \cf0 How to handle it in C++ (Qt):\

\f5\b0\fs32 When saving to or reading from the database, you simply multiply or divide by 100 in your C++ logic:\

\f4\b \strokec2 Writing to the database:
\f5\b0 \strokec2 \

\fs28 \

\fs40 cpp\

\f2\fs28 double priceInDollars = 19.99;\
int priceInCents = static_cast<int>(priceInDollars * 100); // 1999\
\
QSqlQuery query;\
query.prepare("INSERT INTO invoice_items (..., snapshot_unit_price) VALUES (..., :price)");\
query.bindValue(":price", priceInCents);\
query.exec();\

\f5\fs24 Use code with caution.\
